			"Message": "feat(Project): Implement VS Code extension host with full language provider support\n\nComplete the VS Code API compatibility layer across Cocoon, Mountain, and Wind submodules:\n\n**Cocoon:**\n- Implement full languages namespace with 25+ provider registrations (hover, completion, definition, references, code actions, formatting, signature help, semantic tokens, etc.)\n- Each register*Provider assigns unique handle and routes to Mountain via gRPC\n- Implement command registry with local handlers and gRPC routing\n- Add has() and fix inspect() for Workspace configuration\n\n**Mountain:**\n- Expand IPC handlers for storage, notifications, progress, quick input, workspaces, themes, search\n- Add gRPC handlers for commands, window, workspace, secrets, FS operations\n- Implement 20+ language provider registration handlers emitting Tauri events to Sky\n- Complete the extension host contract for basic editor operations\n\n**Wind:**\n- Add Tier 3 services: StorageService, NotificationService, ProgressService, QuickInputService, WorkspacesService, ThemesService, SearchService\n- Integrate all new services into TauriBaseLayer and TauriLiveLayer\n- Add Problem types for proper error handling\n\nThis enables VS Code extensions running in Cocoon to access full LSP functionality including diagnostics, code completion, hover tooltips, refactoring, and semantic analysis.",
			"SHA": "47a03b05aced36f4d9eb6ecad489c8490fa7000f"
		},
