				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Implement output channel events and Terminal/Output services\n\nComplete the terminal and output functionality across Mountain and Wind submodules:\n\n**Mountain:**\n- Implement output channel operations (create, append, appendLine, clear, show) that emit Tauri events to Sky (`sky://output/*`) for frontend rendering\n- Implement get_configuration delegating to ConfigurationProvider for VS Code configuration access\n- This enables VS Code extensions running in Cocoon to interact with output panels\n\n**Wind:**\n- Add TerminalService Live implementation backed by Mountain's TerminalProvider via Tauri IPC\n- Add OutputService for output channel management with CreateChannel, Append, AppendLine, Clear, Show, Dispose methods\n- Update TextFileService to use actual Tauri IPC instead of stub\n\nThis completes the gRPC service contract between Mountain and Cocoon, enabling full output channel support from the extension host while exposing Terminal and Output services in Wind's Effect-TS layer.",
			"SHA": "95ff93d0b42705b2ae19273b9b87fab5772f50c6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:39:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Add terminal IPC handlers and TerminalService interface\n\nAdd coordinated terminal functionality across Mountain and Wind submodules:\n\n**Mountain:**\n- Add Wind IPC handlers for terminal operations (create, sendText, dispose, show, hide) delegating to TerminalProvider\n- Add output channel handlers (create, append, appendLine, clear, show) emitting Tauri events to Sky\n- Add textFile handlers (read, write, save) using tokio::fs for disk I/O\n\n**Wind:**\n- Add TerminalService interface for Effect-TS based service layer\n- Implement methods: CreateTerminal, SendText, Dispose, Show, Hide\n- Add TerminalProblem discriminated union for typed error handling\n\nThis completes the terminal IPC bridge between Wind's service layer and Mountain's native backend, enabling the full terminal lifecycle from the editor UI.",
			"SHA": "79e3cf008128b1f7b5998113db458baf7c8d8a74"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:36:22Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): implement generic request router in process_mountain_request\n\nImplement the generic request handler that routes fs.* and commands.execute methods from Cocoon's FileSystemService. The previous implementation returned \"Method not found\" errors for all requests. Now properly handles: fs.readFile/file:read, fs.writeFile/file:write, fs.stat/file:stat, fs.listDir/fs.readdir/file:readdir, fs.createDir/file:mkdir, fs.delete/file:delete, fs.rename/file:move, and commands.execute. Each method delegates to the appropriate handler or returns a JSON-RPC compatible response.\n\nThis enables Cocoon's generic ProcessCocoonRequest RPC to work with the same operations available via typed gRPC methods, completing the gRPC service contract between Mountain and Cocoon.\n\nRefs: bd2d00daeba4658e3f694681daf253c64403a113, 2d0d95417c08c3a53f30ed7cc029f2723eb7ec17",
			"SHA": "701c7302626eb6767bf8b5d523e610b705d2dc80"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-05T13:34:04Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): implement terminal I/O, secret storage, and UI dialogs in CocoonService\n\nReplace unimplemented stubs with working implementations:\n- Terminal I/O: terminal_input sends bytes to PTY stdin via SendTextToTerminal, close_terminal disposes PTY via DisposeTerminal\n- Secret Storage: get_secret/store_secret/delete_secret delegate to OS keychain via SecretProvider (GetSecret, StoreSecret, DeleteSecret)\n- UI Dialogs: show_quick_pick presents selection list via ShowQuickPick, show_input_box presents text entry via ShowInputBox\n- Terminal Resize: emits Tauri event 'sky://terminal/resize' to Sky for xterm.js canvas resizing\n\nAll operations now properly call their corresponding MountainEnvironment providers instead of returning Status::unimplemented, completing the gRPC service contract between Mountain and Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "bd2d00daeba4658e3f694681daf253c64403a113"
		}
